! Diamond carbon with an ultrasoft pseudopotential -- QE's own
! test-suite/ph_base/c.scf.in, the ground state its `c.phG.in` computes a
! dielectric constant of with `epsil = .true.`.
!
! The second ultrasoft case, and the independent one: a different element, a
! different cutoff pair (27/300 rather than 20/160) and a different lattice
! constant from si-epsilon-us.in, so agreeing on both is not agreeing twice on
! the same arithmetic.
!
! The `nr1`/`nr2`/`nr3` lines of the original are dropped: they force a 32^3 FFT
! grid, which is what `ecutrho = 300` gives here anyway, and pypresso does not
! read them.
 &control
    calculation='scf',
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) =6.74, nat=  2, ntyp= 1,
    ecutwfc = 27.0
    ecutrho = 300.0
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.7
    conv_thr =  1.0d-9
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 C   12.0107  C.pz-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 C  0.00 0.00 0.00
 C  0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS AUTOMATIC
4 4 4 1 1 1
